[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186133284 :answer-field/choices 17592186133285] [:db/retract 17592186133284 :answer-field/choices 17592186133286] [:db/retract 17592186133284 :answer-field/choices 17592186133287] [:db/retract 17592186133284 :answer-field/choices 17592186133288] [:db/retract 17592186133284 :answer-field/choices 17592186133289] {:db/id 17592186134541 :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{e}^{-|x/2|}}{4},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x/2}}{2},\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t/2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}t, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t/2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t/2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{t/2}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x/2}}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t/2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{t/2}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-t/2}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x/2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{-t/2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-x/2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x/2}}{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/2}}{2}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133284 :answer-field/correct "answer-b905210f-a059-572c-8e25-2b36e139ca53" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b905210f-a059-572c-8e25-2b36e139ca53" "answer-128e3b85-4be0-58d5-9120-cf5364e7369e" "answer-82c39e58-8d46-563b-b847-882b5527d6e1" "answer-c09d67cf-c692-53b9-9009-9755c3847a2d" "answer-9b72f51e-b7fa-5eaa-b4a9-881ec5d3b1ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b905210f-a059-572c-8e25-2b36e139ca53" :answer/id #uuid "b905210f-a059-572c-8e25-2b36e139ca53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-128e3b85-4be0-58d5-9120-cf5364e7369e" :answer/id #uuid "128e3b85-4be0-58d5-9120-cf5364e7369e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-x/2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82c39e58-8d46-563b-b847-882b5527d6e1" :answer/id #uuid "82c39e58-8d46-563b-b847-882b5527d6e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-x/2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c09d67cf-c692-53b9-9009-9755c3847a2d" :answer/id #uuid "c09d67cf-c692-53b9-9009-9755c3847a2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-x/2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b72f51e-b7fa-5eaa-b4a9-881ec5d3b1ce" :answer/id #uuid "9b72f51e-b7fa-5eaa-b4a9-881ec5d3b1ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-x/2}}{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129173 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-62a31be5-1f88-5fce-bc3d-c7a604a6e638"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-62a31be5-1f88-5fce-bc3d-c7a604a6e638" :question/id #uuid "62a31be5-1f88-5fce-bc3d-c7a604a6e638" :question/math-academy-id "q-72402" :question/problem "${\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}-{j}^{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}-{j}^{2}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}-{j}^{2})] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(({i}^{2}-{1}^{2})+({i}^{2}-{2}^{2})) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(({i}^{2}-1)+({i}^{2}-4)) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(2{i}^{2}-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}(2{i}^{2}-5) & =(2(1)^{2}-5)+(2(2)^{2}-5)+(2(3)^{2}-5) \\\\  & =-3+3+13 \\\\  & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb74bb6d-eb9e-5168-b33b-f718103e0618"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb74bb6d-eb9e-5168-b33b-f718103e0618" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb74bb6d-eb9e-5168-b33b-f718103e0618" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-135c1c58-72fd-5e33-bb89-e656d31fd58a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f93f673f-1cdf-5fcb-8a52-d4d7a60f012f" "answer-135c1c58-72fd-5e33-bb89-e656d31fd58a" "answer-8f64f0ed-c125-50ec-80b4-0baad2e5331e" "answer-8fdbc633-5f94-527c-beb7-ec30a2b7cea8" "answer-8b3283bc-9a97-5ab1-beab-d6945922e38d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f93f673f-1cdf-5fcb-8a52-d4d7a60f012f" :answer/id #uuid "f93f673f-1cdf-5fcb-8a52-d4d7a60f012f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-135c1c58-72fd-5e33-bb89-e656d31fd58a" :answer/id #uuid "135c1c58-72fd-5e33-bb89-e656d31fd58a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f64f0ed-c125-50ec-80b4-0baad2e5331e" :answer/id #uuid "8f64f0ed-c125-50ec-80b4-0baad2e5331e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fdbc633-5f94-527c-beb7-ec30a2b7cea8" :answer/id #uuid "8fdbc633-5f94-527c-beb7-ec30a2b7cea8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b3283bc-9a97-5ab1-beab-d6945922e38d" :answer/id #uuid "8b3283bc-9a97-5ab1-beab-d6945922e38d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6d3ae80f-587f-5674-9679-5efb33bf0d2c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d3ae80f-587f-5674-9679-5efb33bf0d2c" :question/id #uuid "6d3ae80f-587f-5674-9679-5efb33bf0d2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-157227" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $-3{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3}=0.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3} & =-3[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12+0+2 \\\\ 3+6+4 \\\\ 0+0+10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can reorder the equations in this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-993bd62a-640e-5656-8035-d20d8bad796e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-993bd62a-640e-5656-8035-d20d8bad796e" :answer-field/id #uuid "993bd62a-640e-5656-8035-d20d8bad796e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b1e669dd-ebc9-5d9b-a6c3-bf1f63c51806" :answer-field/choices ["answer-14d3b9a6-b42e-5d81-b5e8-d7e65c357f71" "answer-d63d1670-ebb4-54f4-afea-a48835538de1" "answer-b1e669dd-ebc9-5d9b-a6c3-bf1f63c51806" "answer-5a089876-2b6c-5a99-9e81-d189370977ea" "answer-6e02d051-6b0a-5a1c-8d4f-65d665e53a26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14d3b9a6-b42e-5d81-b5e8-d7e65c357f71" :answer/id #uuid "14d3b9a6-b42e-5d81-b5e8-d7e65c357f71" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d63d1670-ebb4-54f4-afea-a48835538de1" :answer/id #uuid "d63d1670-ebb4-54f4-afea-a48835538de1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1e669dd-ebc9-5d9b-a6c3-bf1f63c51806" :answer/id #uuid "b1e669dd-ebc9-5d9b-a6c3-bf1f63c51806" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a089876-2b6c-5a99-9e81-d189370977ea" :answer/id #uuid "5a089876-2b6c-5a99-9e81-d189370977ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e02d051-6b0a-5a1c-8d4f-65d665e53a26" :answer/id #uuid "6e02d051-6b0a-5a1c-8d4f-65d665e53a26" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157394 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8da6073f-aed1-5284-a635-95231dda9375"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8da6073f-aed1-5284-a635-95231dda9375" :question/id #uuid "8da6073f-aed1-5284-a635-95231dda9375" :question/math-academy-id "q-152896" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=3{x}^{2},\\,0\\le x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e4c5e0e7-c0ac-54ef-a1ca-a2167b6452cc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e4c5e0e7-c0ac-54ef-a1ca-a2167b6452cc" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c5e0e7-c0ac-54ef-a1ca-a2167b6452cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-155ac80b-d257-59db-8d11-526c13b72b8a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-10f69397-caa8-5d90-9585-243065e0aedd